From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: mediatek: serialize the shared QDMA queue window

The page selector and the TX queue counter mode control a shared frame
engine register window. The Ethernet debugfs writer selects a page
before copying user data, so a concurrent statistics read or HNAT
shaper update can redirect writes to another queue.

Use the same IRQ-safe lock for Ethernet and Vendor HNAT transactions.
Select the page only after parsing, keep configuration and counter
reads on their selected page, and restore the original window state
before releasing the lock. Snapshot reset diagnostics before printing.
Keep HNAT reservations and the associated shaper writes together.

Source: Project-original. The affected debugfs writer originates in
commit c8ad16d28d66 ("mediatek sdk:add kernel files"). The HNAT shaper
was checked in the effective Refresh Linux 6.6.159 tree.
Scope: MediaTek QDMA, including MT7987/MT7988 with Vendor HNAT.
Build and hardware validation: pending.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>

